3. Touch controllers — datasheet-sourced interfaces
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  The Zephyr touch adapters (XPT2046 resistive over SPI, FT6336U capacitive
  over I2C) in packages/framework-zephyr/src/display/touch-adapter.ts are
  independently written against Zephyr driver APIs. The register addresses,
  command bytes, and coordinate layouts they use are factual hardware
  interface descriptions taken directly from the XPT2046/ADS7843 and
  FT6336U datasheets; no third-party library was transcribed.

  One convention is borrowed from prior art and noted here for honesty:
  the XPT2046 pen-detect threshold default (raw Z1 threshold of 400) comes
  from the MIT-licensed Arduino XPT2046_Touchscreen library's Z_THRESHOLD
  (Copyright (c) 2015 Paul Stoffregen); it is a tuning constant, not
  creative expression.

  Other touch controllers (STMPE610, GT911, CST816S) have no emitted
  implementation in this toolchain — the framework declines them with a
  clear error.

